        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: કપડું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કપડું — kapḍũ — \"cloth, garment\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "આ કપડું નરમ છે. — ā kapḍũ naram che — \"This cloth is soft.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The plural કપડાં, kapḍā̃, means clothes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કપડું (kapḍũ) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from karpaṭa, \"patched garment, rag\"; CDIAL glosses the Gujarati word \"any garment\" and asks whether it came by way of Hindi (CDIAL 2871)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
            }
