              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દુપટ્ટો — dupaṭṭo — \"scarf, stole\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "તેનો દુપટ્ટો લાલ છે. — teno dupaṭṭo lāl che — \"Her scarf is red.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દુપટ્ટો (dupaṭṭo) is built from du-, \"two\", and paṭṭo, \"strip of cloth\". Under Sanskrit paṭṭa, \"cloth\", which it thinks probably non-Aryan, CDIAL lists the kindred Gujarati pāṭ, \"strip of cloth\", and pāṭo, \"bandage\", but no form of the compound itself (CDIAL 7700)."
            }
          ]
        },
