              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઓઢવું — oḍhvũ — \"to wrap oneself in, to cover oneself\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "શિયાળામાં હું ધાબળો ઓઢું છું. — śiyāḷāmā̃ hũ dhābaḷo oḍhũ chũ — \"In winter I wrap myself in a blanket.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઓઢવું (oḍhvũ) is inherited through Prakrit. It comes from ōḍḍh, \"put on, wear, cover\", a reconstructed form that CDIAL takes to be borrowed from Dravidian, beside Tamil uṭu-, \"to dress\", though it notes that Burrow derives the Tamil verb otherwise (CDIAL 2547)."
            }
          ]
        },
